0. Definitions.

"This License" refers to version 3 of the GNU Affero General Public License.

"Copyright" also means copyright-like laws that apply to other kinds of
works, such as semiconductor masks.

"The Program" refers to any copyrightable work licensed under this
License. Each licensee is addressed as "you". "Licensees" and
"recipients" may be individuals or organizations.

To "modify" a work means to copy from or adapt all or part of the work
in a fashion requiring copyright permission, other than the making of an
auxiliary cross reference tool. The resulting work is called a "modified
version" of the earlier work or a work "based on" the earlier work.

A "covered work" means either the unmodified Program or a work based on
the Program.

To "propagate" a work means to do anything with it that, without
permission, would make you directly or indirectly liable for infringement
under applicable copyright law, except executing it on a computer or
having it done for you. Propagation includes copying, distribution (with
or without the public), making available to the public, and in some cases
other activities that make the work accessible to the public.

To "convey" a work means any kind of propagation that enables other
parties to make copies of it. Mere interaction with a user through a
computer network, with no transfer of a copy, is not conveying.

An "interactive user interface" displays a "License Notice" if it
includes a convenient and prominently visible feature that (1) displays
an appropriate copyright notice, and (2) tells the user that there is no
warranty for the work (except to the extent that warranties are implied
by law), and (3) tells the user that the work is licensed under this
License and how to view a copy of this License. If the interface is
presented by the one party, the user may see the License Notice on the
interface itself; if presented by another, the user may see it on the
other party's computer, or the user may be told to visit the URL where
the License Notice can be found.

1. Source Code.

The "source code" for a work means the preferred form of the work for
making modifications to it. "Object code" means any non-source form of a
work.

A "User Product" is either (1) a "consumer product", which means any
tangible personal property that is normally used for personal, family, or
household purposes, or (2) anything designed or sold for incorporation
into dwellings. "Installation Information" for a User Product means any
methods, procedures, authorization codes, or other information required
to install and execute modified versions of the work in that User Product
from a modified version of the object code, in such a way that the
modified version can execute in the same manner and perform the same
functions as the original version.

