6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms of
sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the machine-readable
source code under the terms of this License in one of these ways: (a)
Convey the object code in, and with, a physical medium (including a
durable storage medium) that includes the corresponding source code; (b)
Convey the object code in, and with, a written offer to provide the
corresponding source code; (c) Convey individual copies of the object
code with a copy of the corresponding source code on a durable storage
medium; (d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (including a network server) and offering equivalent access to the
corresponding source code at no additional charge; (e) Convey the object
code using peer-to-peer transmission, provided you inform other peers
where the object code and the corresponding source code are available.

If you convey an object code work under section 6d, you must give
recipients a copy of the corresponding source code no later than when
you give them the object code, and you must make it available for at
least the term of the license. If you convey an object code work using
peer-to-peer transmission under section 6e, the offer of equivalent
access to the corresponding source code must be available for as long as
the object code is available.

